{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> And He returned there until I give you. A sage in Spain said that the first tablets, which were the work of Elohim — the meaning is that they were created ready-made according to the measure of the Ark — for the second ones too were the work of Elohim, since He creates all; only Moses prepared them, for preparation is called \"making,\" as in \"and he hurried to make it\" (Genesis 18:7). And because it is written \"tablets of stone\" [לוחות אבן] in the singular and not \"stones\" [אבנים] as he mentioned regarding the second ones — but behold, I showed him: \"when I went up the mountain to take the tablets of stone\" [לקחת שני לוחות האבנים] (Deuteronomy 9:9), and he mentioned it three times — therefore he explained \"tablets of the stone\" to mean that they were of the category of stone, not of wood. The Gaon [Saadia] said that \"which I have written\" is joined to \"tablets of stone,\" and not to \"the Torah and the commandment,\" for HaShem wrote only the Ten Statements. And he explained <b>the Torah</b> as the written Torah, <b>and the commandment</b> as the oral Torah, for all the commandments were given to Moses at Sinai during the days he stood on the mountain, as it is written: \"And you here, stand with Me\" (Deuteronomy 5:28). And in my opinion, the Torah is the first utterance and the fifth, and the commandment is the eighth statement:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון as the Gaon [Saadia] per standard convention; the final clause about 'the first utterance and the fifth' and 'the eighth statement' refers to the Decalogue but Ibn Ezra leaves the identification cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:03.644373266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}